comments[20]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-03T11:14:27.152Z","harness:codex","Duplicate check 2026-08-03: searched all statuses for recurring issues history CI gate, defect recurrence mining, closed issues generate regression tests, issue pattern CI before push, and historical defect taxonomy quality gate. Existing items own individual quality gates and incidents; none owns history-derived recurrence families plus shared local/hosted check selection."
  "2026-08-07T11:29:32.973Z","harness:claude-code","Recurrence census measured 2026-08-07 over all 2,007 terminal items and their 634 terminal Issues. This is offered as the concrete backfill input the acceptance criteria ask for: the families below are derived from the record rather than proposed from intuition, and each is stated with the evidence that would let a family be defined and a gate be chosen.\n\n## Recurrence by source file — distinct terminal items that linked each file\n\n| items | file |\n|---|---|\n| 247 | src/cli/main.ts |\n| 147 | src/sdk/cli-contracts.ts |\n| 110 | src/cli/commands/completion.ts |\n| 105 | src/sdk/index.ts |\n| 91 | src/cli/commands/create.ts |\n| 76 | src/cli/commands/update.ts |\n| 75 | src/core/extensions/loader.ts |\n| 67 | src/cli/help-content.ts |\n| 65 | src/mcp/server.ts |\n| 65 | src/sdk/runtime.ts |\n\nThe distribution is the finding, not the ranking. Twelve percent of every closed and canceled item in this tracker touched one file. The top five are, almost exactly, the sites the contributor guidance enumerates as the mandatory replication set when a command is added or changed: the command barrel and entrypoint, the contract table, completions, the SDK surface, and the create path. The recurrence hot spots are therefore not risky code — they are the places a single logical change must be written more than once, and the recurring defect is a change applied at some sites and not all.\n\nThat reframes the family. It is not \"main.ts is fragile\". It is **multi-site wiring incompleteness**, its trigger signal is a diff that touches a strict subset of a declared replication set, and its gate is deterministic and local: derive the replication set from the contract table rather than from prose, and fail a change that leaves it partially written. Ruling O applies directly — the replication set is currently a checklist in a markdown file, which is enforcement by prose. The single-source-of-surface-tiering work is the structural fix and should be recorded as this family's canonical owner rather than a related item.\n\nA second, compounding observation: the highest-recurrence file in the project is also the one nearest its size gate, at 99 percent of the 3,400-line cap. Recurrence density and cap proximity are being tracked by two unrelated items and neither reads the other's number. A file that is both the most-changed and the least-extensible in the corpus is the highest-value decomposition target the record can identify, and the recurrence index should expose that join.\n\n## Recurrence by defect family — terminal Issues matching each title signature\n\n| issues | family |\n|---|---|\n| 125 | flag and option contract, unknown-option recovery |\n| 94 | extension and package install, activation |\n| 77 | lock, concurrency, race, stale state |\n| 72 | release, publish, registry boundary |\n| 62 | output shape, projection, token cost |\n| 46 | schema, type, status customization |\n| 45 | history, hash chain, drift, restore |\n| 43 | graph and dependency edge semantics |\n| 42 | search, index, vector staleness |\n| 35 | recovery and refusal message quality |\n| 28 | Windows and cross-platform path or process |\n| 18 | test-harness determinism and flake |\n\nSignatures overlap and 191 terminal issues match none, so these are lower bounds and the residual is large enough that clustering must be evidence-driven rather than keyword-driven in the real implementation. Two families are worth calling out against the backfill list already recorded on this item.\n\nThe flag and option contract family is the largest at 125 and is not named in the current backfill scope. It is also the family with the most deterministic available gate, because the contract table already enumerates every flag and the conformance work already proposes a lexicon; a family here would mostly be wiring an existing contract into a blocking check rather than inventing a detector.\n\nThe concurrency family at 77 is the one where a local deterministic gate is genuinely unavailable, which is why the fault-and-concurrency simulation harness is its correct required check rather than a static rule. Recording it that way matters: the family model should be able to say that a family's required check is a seeded simulation, not only a lint or a test, or the model will under-cover exactly the defects that cost the most.\n\n## Suggested first families, in the order the evidence supports\n\nMulti-site wiring incompleteness — largest measured recurrence, deterministic gate, contract-derived trigger, and it subsumes part of the flag-contract family.\nFlag and option contract divergence — largest issue family, existing contract to gate against.\nRelease and registry boundary — 72 issues and the only family whose escapes are visible to users of the published artifact rather than to contributors.\nConcurrency and stale state — smaller, but the family whose required check must be a simulation, which is the modelling capability this item should prove early rather than late."
  "2026-08-15T13:57:03.527Z","harness:codex","Current recurrence input 2026-08-15: three newly discovered GitHub regressions map to established escape families rather than new umbrellas: pm-2qvq7a is a complete-result/output-budget contract escape, pm-zno2iu is hosted Node-platform/nightly coverage drift, and pm-mcxk8v is destructive bulk-mutation preview safety. Feed their exact reproductions, linked files/tests, causal signatures, and negative controls into the recurrence corpus. The shared SDK artifact should select bounded local checks and broader hosted checks from the same family definitions, prove each seeded failure is detectable, and record population adequacy so a passing fixture cannot hide the escaped property."
  "2026-08-16T19:05:23.352Z","harness:codex","Evidence linkage: associated the benchmark harness test that validates deterministic full/incremental indexing, threshold failures, JSON/human projections, invalid scales, and memory clamping."
  "2026-08-16T19:27:28.816Z","harness:codex","Completion evidence 2026-08-16: public SDK/CLI/generic transport selects 2 explainable families for assurance-action.ts, returns shared local and hosted checks plus a 318-token cost receipt, and works from the packed artifact. Deterministic benchmark PASS at 1,000,000 items: 11,617 ms full, 20 ms incremental, 25,252,216-byte heap delta, 1,009 indexed after a 1,000-item change, within 30s/1s/768MiB ceilings. Linked tests passed 20/20. Full repository suite passed 7,437/7,437 with exact 100/100/100/100 coverage."
  "2026-08-16T19:39:47.463Z","harness:codex","Release-gate evidence: the installed guide-shell/changelog topology exposed five previously unbudgeted help surfaces and raised context help from a 2,886-byte ceiling to 2,967 measured bytes. Regenerated 10% ceilings, then deliberately retained the prior optional search-advanced and reindex ceilings so one extension topology cannot erase another topology’s ratchets. Current token gate passes 85 surfaces."
  "2026-08-16T19:59:47.281Z","harness:codex","Final pre-commit release evidence: the complete release gate passed repository assurance, package boundary/parity, surface replication, tracker/graph/record assurance, 85 token surfaces, 511 test files with 7,437 tests, exact 100/100/100/100 coverage, version synchronization, tracked-file secret scanning, packed npx smoke, and the 88-command package-first dogfood suite. The sole terminal failure was the intentional fail-closed Greptile precondition 'there are no committed code changes to review against main'; the gate must be rerun against the committed exact head. Tracker validation reports zero history drift and zero storage-integrity failures; 295 legacy closed-item resolution warnings are pre-existing backlog, while every item closed by this delivery has complete resolution metadata."
  "2026-08-16T20:01:00.435Z","harness:codex","Delivery PR: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/pull/1043 at initial implementation head 13402a50938cf90d3e8d84b0a017fcd857a54f3e. The PR body links the canonical PM records on main and carries the exact verification, compatibility, security, benchmark, and manual acceptance evidence."
  "2026-08-16T20:15:32.997Z","harness:codex","Review round 1 inventory at head b59fe3c324c90a0b3d2da7cb9b1bce46d1bc1001: CodeRabbit posted 14 actionable inline findings; Sourcery was provider-rate-limited; hosted static CI found a credential-shaped test string at boundary-fixtures.spec.ts:105. Active remediation covers structural input validation, check-contract validity, boundary path containment and evidence counts, selected-scope reporting, incremental reuse/determinism, glob compilation bounds, AST-based producer census, assurance limit/error semantics, and lifecycle-safe test spies. The transport index-cache suggestion will be evaluated against correct invalidation guarantees rather than accepted speculatively."
  "2026-08-16T21:10:56.627Z","harness:codex","Review remediation evidence 2026-08-16: all 14 CodeRabbit findings and the hosted credential-shape failure are implemented. The full sandboxed suite passes 7,438/7,438 with exact statements 54,243/54,243, branches 40,291/40,291, functions 11,161/11,161, and lines 52,363/52,363; jscpd reports 0 clones across 1,020 files; security scan and the 4-captured/4-waived, 6-family defect evidence gate pass. The million-item deterministic repeat passes at 20,149 ms full, 32 ms sparse incremental, and 44,778,576 bytes heap within 30s/1s/768MiB ceilings. Import-cost investigation compared exact pre-fix b59fe3c32 and current bundles under the same loaded host: aggregate means 378.4 ms base vs 374.9 ms current and governance 269.3 ms base vs 274.0 ms current, demonstrating no review-fix regression; the unchanged absolute ratchet currently fails both versions under load average 8-11, so its budget was preserved for clean hosted verification."
  "2026-08-16T21:31:45.798Z","harness:codex","Review round 2 inventory at exact head 94b317e68: all hosted checks passed, while CodeRabbit identified 17 new threads across acceptance metadata, custom-field semantic validation, missing Git boundary evidence, incremental oracle completeness, recovery field coverage/parser correctness/complexity/determinism, cache memory bounds, waiver and boundary parser semantics, recurrence sorting/tag/timestamp fail-closed behavior, and mutation-relevant cache tests. Reopened only this canonical item; each finding is being verified against current code before mutation."
  "2026-08-16T22:20:49.655Z","harness:codex","Review round 2 remediation evidence 2026-08-17: implemented semantic custom-field schemas for escape_class and gate_evidence; added captured/redacted Git rev-parse evidence; strengthened the million-item oracle against a rebuilt updated corpus; added fallback_candidates and next_best_command recovery contracts; replaced lexical recovery scans with a structural object-member census that excludes types, destructuring, labels, comments, strings, templates, and regex; precomputed line offsets and code-unit ordering; hashed process-cache item fingerprints; counted only valid live waivers; rejected non-object boundary rows; filtered non-string tags; and governed post-epoch defects with invalid completion timestamps using closed_at compatibility and explicit pre-epoch grandfathering. Full repository suite: 511 files, 7,443 tests, exact statements 54,421/54,421, branches 40,486/40,486, functions 11,181/11,181, lines 52,528/52,528. ESLint strict complexity and jscpd 0 clones pass. Million-item repeat: 16,649 ms full, 28 ms incremental, 56,283,024-byte heap delta, deterministic. Manual packed acceptance in /tmp/pm-cli-review-round2-Vycl7h proved invalid enum and incomplete waiver refusals, valid structured persistence, and npx plus bunx --bun version 2026.8.16. The repository negative control failed exactly on invalid captured evidence and missing defect evidence."
  "2026-08-16T22:25:50.931Z","harness:codex","Linked-test execution note: the direct exact-coverage command passed 7,443 tests at 100/100/100/100, but the PM-linked wrapper later failed in output transport with Node UNKNOWN synchronous write before coverage reporting. This is not treated as a product or test failure. The distinct, all-status duplicate-checked recurrence is pm-giks4s, linked discovered_from this item and recurs_from the two completed EAGAIN fixes. Removed the unsuitable unbounded linked command while preserving its immutable failed-run receipt; the three bounded linked gates remain authoritative PM-run checks."
  "2026-08-16T22:29:32.268Z","harness:codex","Canonical linked-test receipt 2026-08-17: schema-isolated PM execution passed all 3 linked commands. Focused SDK/CLI tests passed 21/21; recurrence benchmark passed at 1,000,000 items with full=17,580 ms, incremental=27 ms, 57,000,408-byte heap delta, deterministic fingerprint; boundary/census/evidence tests passed 19/19. Execution context reported mismatch_detected=false and no real tracker items copied. The separate high-volume regular-file output-capture recurrence is tracked open and unclaimed as pm-giks4s; it does not invalidate the direct exact-coverage receipt."
  "2026-08-16T22:50:19.081Z","harness:codex","Hosted CI remediation 2026-08-17: exact-head Gates (static) failed only on evaluateDefectGateEvidence CodeFactor complexity 19>16 and a stale src/sdk/schema.ts private-SDK allowlist entry. Shared terminal-defect selection reduced complexity within 16; the stale exception was removed because schema.ts is now public. Direct static-quality gate reports ok=true, 100% source/export/member docstrings, zero codefactor violations, and zero SDK boundary violations. Decision pm-4smp5b authorized forward-only schema/fields.json reconciliation; _workspace verification and history-drift validation now report zero mismatches."
  "2026-08-16T23:08:50.698Z","harness:codex","Final local exact-state verification 2026-08-17: pnpm quality:static completed exit 0 across repository-static-quality, package boundary, SDK contract parity, surface replication, tracker-context-quality, gate registry, SDK surface/import costs, CLI transport floor, graph composition, and record integrity. Related-to ceiling restored by replacing shallow links with typed verifies edges. pm-changelog registry latest and installed version are both 2026.8.16; CHANGELOG.md regenerated and check mode is unchanged at 2,119 closed items."
  "2026-08-17T00:26:20.497Z","harness:codex","Final review-remediation evidence 2026-08-17: resolved the third CodeRabbit inventory across pre-release trigger coverage, workspace decision reconciliation, symlink/canonical boundary containment, fail-closed recursive value-schema normalization, contract-derived refusal fields, invalid-source recovery, prototype-safe contracts, bounded cache semantics, non-string boundary ids, malformed linked-file metadata, undated terminal recurrence governance, real CLI invalid-JSON rejection, positive timestamp/waiver controls, lifecycle-safe JSON.parse spies, assurance risk transport metadata, and complete operator documentation. All four PM-linked commands pass: 22 functional/integration tests; the deterministic million-item benchmark at 15,051 ms full, 35 ms incremental, 40,936,840-byte heap delta; 21 boundary/refusal negative controls; and 71 schema/workflow contract tests. Full repository coverage passes 511 files and 7,447 tests at exact 100/100/100/100 (54,494 statements, 40,564 branches, 11,204 functions, 52,596 lines). Static assurance passes with 100% source/export/member docstrings, zero CodeFactor violations, zero SDK boundary drift, and passing absence, token, calibration, docs, defect-evidence, graph, and record-integrity gates. Secret scan, 1,408-file package artifact gate, and 88-command package-first temporary-directory dogfood all pass."
  "2026-08-17T00:47:59.762Z","harness:codex","Review round 4 inventory at exact head 87d7bd1d0: all hosted executable checks passed; CodeRabbit posted 17 findings spanning stale historical evidence references, RFC 3339/UTC timestamp semantics, one_of evaluation bounds, recurrence policy nonempty checks, malformed tracker metadata, tokenizer completeness, cache-hit costs, and test diagnostic isolation. Reopened and claimed only this canonical feature; PM evidence corrections are being applied through public mutation commands, never direct history edits."
  "2026-08-17T01:01:38.109Z","harness:codex","Review round 4 remediation: corrected historical acceptance metadata through pm mutations; enforced calendar-valid RFC 3339 date-time values and UTC waiver expiries; bounded one_of matching; completed arrow-regex recovery parsing and removed redundant census state; rejected empty recurrence check arrays and malformed item types; improved integration diagnostics; split composite transport and recovery-census tests into isolated behavioral cases; and replaced full PM-record cache serialization with a shared recurrence-signal projection that hashes only the fields the sparse index consumes. Focused verification passes 132/132 tests; TypeScript and the strict static-quality gate pass with 100% source/export/member docstrings and zero complexity or SDK-boundary violations."
  "2026-08-17T01:15:11.722Z","harness:codex","Exact review-round verification 2026-08-17: full sandboxed coverage passed 511/511 files and 7,454/7,454 tests at statements 54,503/54,503, branches 40,589/40,589, functions 11,205/11,205, lines 52,604/52,604. Repository quality:static, package boundary/parity, surface replication, tracker-context, gate registry, SDK surface/import costs, CLI transport floor, graph composition, record integrity, secrets scan, and the 1,410-file packed artifact gate all passed. All five PM-linked commands passed; the million-item recurrence benchmark completed in 15,339 ms full and 26 ms incremental with 40,426,232-byte heap delta and deterministic identity. Manual package-first SDK acceptance from /tmp/pm-cli-round4-dWJfg9 installed the tarball and proved cache lifecycle true -> false -> false across mutation and deletion on version 2026.8.16."
notes[2]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-14T10:20:07.110Z","harness:codex","Defect-recurrence CI design. Mine closed incidents and fixes into normalized failure signatures keyed by violated contract, root cause, affected surface, triggering input, missing observation, and the earliest gate that could have stopped escape. Cluster only after preserving canonical incident identities; every promoted pattern creates or links one minimal negative control and one positive control, with the test linked back by verifies and discovered_from edges. Route fast deterministic controls to author-time or pre-push verification, broader property and compatibility matrices to hosted CI, and production-only signals to scheduled or release gates. Distinguish product regressions from infrastructure failures and flakes with rerun and timing evidence; never turn cancellation, silence, or rate limiting into approval. Measure recurrence rate, escaped-defect rate, time-to-detection, false-positive burden, flake rate, and coverage of resolved patterns. A resolved incident pattern may leave the gate only through a recorded superseding decision, so protection does not disappear when the original item closes."
  "2026-08-16T10:40:21.541Z","harness:claude-code","Measured recurrence family, 2026-08-16 — \"the check enumerates a set it maintains instead of the set the artifact defines\". Scanned all 1,547 Issue and Task items, open and terminal.\n\nSeven instances, six already fixed and one found today:\n\n  pm-b84irw   closed   Measure source replication against an independently discovered denominator\n  pm-te6elw   closed   SDK completeness asserted by a 10-case curated array against 85 declared actions\n  pm-1jrdri   closed   The rendered command surface is not a subset of the contracted surface\n  pm-6j7r1a   closed   The runtime contract enumeration is not closed over the surface it can resolve\n  pm-xpumg4   closed   The boundary gate proves the CLI stopped importing private core and never proves it only imports the published SDK\n  pm-7wx1f9   closed   Nested workspace snapshot and help paths are enumerated but not resolvable\n  pm-suhxny   open     The public-surface gate enumerates its own hand-written entrypoint list; two published code exports ship ungoverned\n\nEvery one of them has the same three-part shape. A machine-readable artifact defines a set to the outside world — the export map, the workflow files, the command registration, the action table. A checker keeps its own enumeration of that set. The checker proves its list against the artifact and never proves the artifact against its list, so the check is complete over its own belief and silent about everything the artifact gained since the belief was written.\n\nTwo properties make this family worth detecting specifically rather than treating each instance as a one-off.\n\nIt fails open and it fails silently. Every one of the seven passed green while the gap existed. The failure is not a wrong answer, it is a correct answer to a smaller question, which is invisible in a pass/fail verdict and only appears when someone computes the denominator independently.\n\nIt recurs at the moment of growth. Nothing breaks when the hand list is written; the divergence begins the first time the artifact gains an entry. So the defect is introduced by a change that is unrelated to the checker, by an author who has no reason to look at it, which is precisely the situation review does not catch.\n\n## The detectable signature\n\nFor pm-1qkivy this family is a concrete first target, because the signature is narrow enough to detect without drowning in false positives:\n\n- a module under scripts/ or src/ that declares a frozen literal collection (Object.freeze over an object or array, or a `new Set([...])` of string literals), and\n- reads a structured artifact in the same function or module — package.json, a workflows directory, a generated contract table, a registry JSON — and\n- indexes into the artifact using members of the literal, rather than iterating the artifact.\n\nThat third clause is the discriminator. `for (const key of MY_LIST) lookup(artifact[key])` is the defect; `for (const key of Object.keys(artifact)) require(MY_MAP[key])` is the correct shape.\n\n## The positive control already in the repository\n\nscripts/release/gate-registry.mjs implements the correct shape. `discoverWorkflowGates` parses every file under .github/workflows and returns the real job identifiers, then `validateGateRegistry` checks both directions explicitly: `pipeline:<id>:unregistered` when the artifact has an entry the registry lacks, and `pipeline:<id>:not_enforced` when the registry has an entry the artifact lacks. The hand-maintained registry is annotation on a derived set, never the enumeration.\n\nThat gives any detector a same-repository positive control and a same-repository negative control, which is what pm-rtn5h6's escape ratchet asks every new gate to carry. It also means the fix for each instance is a known refactor rather than a design question.\n\n## Cost of the escapes\n\nSix shipped fixes for one shape. The seventh escaped into a published artifact: 2026.8.16 on npm resolves `@unbrained/pm-cli/cli` to a declaration file exporting 86 internal helpers, and the surface gate that exists to prevent exactly that reported \"0 classified changes\" for it. Installing the published tarball with bun and importing the entrypoint returns both symbols, typed.\n\nRecorded on pm-1qkivy as a detector target and on pm-ouyq3n as a worked example of a recurrence the current relationship lexicon cannot express: these seven items are seven unrelated nodes to any graph walk, and the only thing tying them together today is this note."
learnings[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-16T19:27:29.470Z","harness:codex","Compile stable typed signals into a sparse fingerprinted index once, then bind cursors to that immutable identity and update only changed item ids; this keeps change-risk receipts bounded without weakening deterministic local/hosted gate parity."
